{"title":"Ishika's Leaf Mystery","gradeSubjectTag":"Class 5 · Science · Photosynthesis and Chlorophyll","readMinutes":2,"scenes":[{"label":"hook","text":"Ishika was sitting in her grandmother's garden on a sunny afternoon, surrounded by bright green leaves. She picked up a leaf and held it to the light, wondering why every leaf she'd ever seen was the same green colour."},{"label":"problem","text":"'Dadi, why are all the leaves green?' Ishika asked. Her grandmother smiled but admitted she didn't know. Ishika wanted to understand this mystery so badly that she spent the whole evening searching, but no one could give her a clear answer."},{"label":"mathMoment","text":"The next day, Ishika's science teacher explained that inside every leaf lives a special green substance called chlorophyll. When sunlight touches the leaf, chlorophyll catches the light and uses it to make food for the plant—a process called photosynthesis. The chlorophyll absorbs red and blue colours of sunlight very well, but it bounces back the green light, so green is the colour our eyes see."},{"label":"wrapUp","text":"Ishika ran back to her grandmother's garden and looked at the leaves with wonder. Now she understood: the leaves weren't green because they wanted to be—they were green because chlorophyll was hard at work inside them, catching sunlight to feed the plant. She picked a green leaf and whispered, 'Thank you, chlorophyll, for feeding the garden.'"}],"visual":null,"equations":[],"tryTogether":{"question":"If a leaf has chlorophyll that catches red and blue light but bounces back green light, what colour would you see if you looked at the leaf?","answer":"You would see green, because the green light bounces back to your eyes."},"parentPrompt":"Next time you're outside, pick a green leaf together and talk about all the invisible work chlorophyll is doing inside it to keep the plant alive.","concept_key":"c5-science-chlorophyll-photosynthesis","scene_prompt":"A curious girl discovers why the sun-loving leaves in her garden all wear the same bright colour."}
